## Black French Tips for Bold, Edgy Fall Nails

A milky white base, almost invisible against pale skin, with a sharp black tip laid on top. That single contrast is why black tips photograph better than nearly any other option among **fall french tip nails** this season. There is no ambiguity in the shape, no question about where the tip starts.

Black reads bold, but it does not have to read harsh. A glossy finish over a nude or milky base softens the contrast just enough to keep it wearable for daily life. Matte black, by comparison, pushes the look further toward editorial and away from everyday, so the finish choice is really a decision about how loud you want the color to feel.

This is the color for someone who has already worn brown and burgundy in past falls and wants more edge without stepping into full nail art territory. Black tips keep the French structure intact, meaning shape and placement stay classic even though the color is anything but.

A few nail artists are pairing black tips with a single thin silver or gold line at the smile line for fall, a subtle way to add dimension without a second full color. It is a five-minute addition at most salons.

