## What Nail Shape Is Best for Fall French Tips?

Almond and squoval are the two shapes that carry a fall-colored French tip best, with almond giving the tip a slightly elongated, elegant line and squoval giving it a cleaner, more graphic edge. Square nails can absolutely wear French tips too, they just change the visual effect from soft to sharp rather than one being objectively better than the other.

Most people assume it backward: shape does not decide color, color decides shape. Once you have picked chocolate brown, burgundy, black, or olive, the shape either amplifies or mutes that choice. A darker, moodier color like black or burgundy on squoval or square reads graphic and architectural. That same color on almond softens into something more refined.

Coffin and stiletto shapes work too, but they change how much tip color you see. A coffin shape's wider tip gives tortoiseshell or a deep French more surface area to show pattern and depth than a narrow almond tip would.

There is no single correct shape for **fall french tip nails**. What matters is pairing shape and color intentionally rather than picking them separately. A wide, dramatic burgundy tip on a narrow almond shape fights itself. That same burgundy on squoval or coffin has room to breathe.

